p/next "step-1ef6544a-325c-5bf4-ad8a-26a2a5872b84" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1ef6544a-325c-5bf4-ad8a-26a2a5872b84" :step/id #uuid "1ef6544a-325c-5bf4-ad8a-26a2a5872b84" :step/content 17592186348337 :step/next "step-8f674b71-819d-50c4-9b12-f63f0a340a25" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8f674b71-819d-50c4-9b12-f63f0a340a25" :step/id #uuid "8f674b71-819d-50c4-9b12-f63f0a340a25" :step/content 17592186262946 :step/next "step-fe57e0c2-67ad-59f1-9759-bf1442fb9137" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fe57e0c2-67ad-59f1-9759-bf1442fb9137" :step/id #uuid "fe57e0c2-67ad-59f1-9759-bf1442fb9137" :step/content 17592186262961 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186095580 :answer-field/choices 17592186095584] [:db/retract 17592186095580 :answer-field/choices 17592186095585] [:db/retract 17592186095580 :answer-field/choices 17592186095581] [:db/retract 17592186095580 :answer-field/choices 17592186095582] [:db/retract 17592186095580 :answer-field/choices 17592186095583] {:db/id 17592186097276 :question/problem "$\\int {cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x) \\\\ {cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cot}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)\\text{d}x & =\\int ({csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)\\text{d}x-\\int 1\\cdot \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186095580 :answer-field/correct "answer-2f1ecc2b-8f38-5a56-b452-79a084abe981" :answer-field/choices ["answer-381e7704-3610-52d0-943d-11d2f5db4582" "answer-741642b8-40a1-5ddc-a062-46c687fc6284" "answer-da75dca0-cf1f-53aa-85b2-c756cac65ae8" "answer-120a969c-c232-5a6a-9ebc-f3876756aa9d" "answer-2f1ecc2b-8f38-5a56-b452-79a084abe981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-381e7704-3610-52d0-943d-11d2f5db4582" :answer/id #uuid "381e7704-3610-52d0-943d-11d2f5db4582" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-741642b8-40a1-5ddc-a062-46c687fc6284" :answer/id #uuid "741642b8-40a1-5ddc-a062-46c687fc6284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da75dca0-cf1f-53aa-85b2-c756cac65ae8" :answer/id #uuid "da75dca0-cf1f-53aa-85b2-c756cac65ae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-120a969c-c232-5a6a-9ebc-f3876756aa9d" :answer/id #uuid "120a969c-c232-5a6a-9ebc-f3876756aa9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)+x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f1ecc2b-8f38-5a56-b452-79a084abe981" :answer/id #uuid "2f1ecc2b-8f38-5a56-b452-79a084abe981" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-x)-x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d59d88c8-9c62-51d9-bd12-48f5c362cc67" "question-43534459-b512-57ce-a24a-a07661c93918"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d59d88c8-9c62-51d9-bd12-48f5c362cc67" :question/id #uuid "d59d88c8-9c62-51d9-bd12-48f5c362cc67" :question/math-academy-id "q-352652" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x+1}{{sec}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x+1}{{sec}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2d075a9-50ba-561b-90ab-b8b2901e72d8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2d075a9-50ba-561b-90ab-b8b2901e72d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2d075a9-50ba-561b-90ab-b8b2901e72d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8d681392-0578-56c7-9fe2-42e3d7339e02" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8d681392-0578-56c7-9fe2-42e3d7339e02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d681392-0578-56c7-9fe2-42e3d7339e02" :answer/id #uuid "8d681392-0578-56c7-9fe2-42e3d7339e02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-43534459-b512-57ce-a24a-a07661c93918" :question/id #uuid "43534459-b512-57ce-a24a-a07661c93918" :question/math-academy-id "q-352679" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3/2}\\frac{3{x}^{2}{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So, we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3/2}\\frac{3{x}^{2}{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3/2}\\frac{3{x}^{2}{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3/2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{3/2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{\\,3}-{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{8}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f5f4070c-c95c-5ed1-901f-4528153978ca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f5f4070c-c95c-5ed1-901f-4528153978ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5f4070c-c95c-5ed1-901f-4528153978ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b1be8b56-e0bc-581a-9ccb-692511badae8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b1be8b56-e0bc-581a-9ccb-692511badae8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1be8b56-e0bc-581a-9ccb-692511badae8" :answer/id #uuid "b1be8b56-e0bc-581a-9ccb-692511badae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-90eec35c-ddf7-5ea5-a497-a880f0806d02" :activity/id #uuid "90eec35c-ddf7-5ea5-a497-a880f0806d02" :activity/title "Integration Using the Pythagorean Identities" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048717 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-7d91831c-a36e-5666-be56-1ca4b1240a11" "step-31f912e5-8a70-534e-ac44-c11588546e18" "step-eb2c7d86-1bd5-50b3-96ee-f7bfe6f66eba" "step-32479e06-331d-52b3-9dbf-e9c2865786c4" "step-7c4b1db8-dd3d-50f2-843b-a8e34b2a05de"] :activity/first-step "step-7d91831c-a36e-5666-be56-1ca4b1240a11" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7d91831c-a36e-5666-be56-1ca4b1240a11" :step/id #uuid "7d91831c-a36e-5666-be56-1ca4b1240a11" :step/content 17592186097276 :step/next "step-31f912e5-8a70-534e-ac44-c11588546e18" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-31f912e5-8a70-534e-ac44-c11588546e18" :step/id #uuid "31f912e5-8a70-534e-ac44-c11588546e18" :step/content 17592186250269 :step/next "step-eb2c7d86-1bd5-50b3-96ee-f7bfe6f66eba" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eb2c7d86-1bd5-50b3-96ee-f7bfe6f66eba" :step/id #uuid "eb2c7d86-1bd5-50b3-96ee-f7bfe6f66eba" :step/content "question-d59d88c8-9c62-51d9-bd12-48f5c362cc67" :step/next "step-32479e06-331d-52b3-9dbf-e9c2865786c4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-32479e06-331d-52b3-9dbf-e9c2865786c4" :step/id #uuid "32479e06-331d-52b3-9dbf-e9c2865786c4" :step/content "question-43534459-b512-57ce-a24a-a07661c93918" :step/next "step-7c4b1db8-dd3d-50f2-843b-a8e34b2a05de" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7c4b1db8-dd3d-50f2-843b-a8e34b2a05de" :step/id #uuid "7c4b1db8-dd3d-50f2-843b-a8e34b2a05de" :step/content 17592186321026 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129312 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2dd7bee1-71b3-5685-9b9f-df2041d5d283"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2dd7bee1-71b3-5685-9b9f-df2041d5d283" :question/id #uuid "2dd7bee1-71b3-5685-9b9f-df2041d5d283" :question/math-academy-id "q-79732" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=2 \\\\ {c}_{1}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n5\\cdot 6+{c}_{2}=2\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-28.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution for the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+(-28)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}30 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}-28 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8bc94f58-c888-5f48-8bc9-61a9a2954b43"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8bc94f58-c888-5f48-8bc9-61a9a2954b43" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc94f58-c888-5f48-8bc9-61a9a2954b43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a00c0b88-91a7-5321-9fb1-4c0eb83e8718" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a00c0b88-91a7-5321-9fb1-4c0eb83e8718" "answer-0960efec-d285-5cdd-9e4c-60cdf590887c" "answer-75efba6a-e437-5328-8072-189d93667b50" "answer-baae230c-b658-5758-b99c-87c465155740" "answer-eb9a0dee-ec6c-54ab-9bd5-bc8eda85ad1e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a00c0b88-91a7-5321-9fb1-4c0eb83e8718" :answer/id #uuid "a00c0b88-91a7-5321-9fb1-4c0eb83e8718" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}30 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}-28 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0960efec-d285-5cdd-9e4c-60cdf590887c" :answer/id #uuid "0960efec-d285-5cdd-9e4c-60cdf590887c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}30 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75efba6a-e437-5328-8072-189d93667b50" :answer/id #uuid "75efba6a-e437-5328-8072-189d93667b50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}35 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}-28 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-baae230c-b658-5758-b99c-87c465155740" :answer/id #uuid "baae230c-b658-5758-b99c-87c465155740" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb9a0dee-ec6c-54ab-9bd5-bc8eda85ad1e" :answer/id #uuid "eb9a0dee-ec6c-54ab-9bd5-bc8eda85ad1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}28 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198448 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-dfb0578c-1343-53e2-a376-085feaa6ce26"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-dfb0578c-1343-53e2-a376-085feaa6ce26" :question/id #uuid "dfb0578c-1343-53e2-a376-085feaa6ce26" :question/math-academy-id "q-140566" :question/problem "Let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Find $‖Q(x)‖$, where $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe linear transformation $Q$ being orthogonal is equivalent to the following:\n\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nIn this case, since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖Q(x)‖ & =‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-131118e0-de48-5f9d-ada7-20da3689be40"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-131118e0-de48-5f9d-ada7-20da3689be40" :answer-field/id #uuid "131118e0-de48-5f9d-ada7-20da3689be40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-00b575c8-36c5-5013-80f6-ee1498a6faf2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01915aac-1c2e-585b-999e-bd689a77b856" "answer-d11c7d00-ca24-5099-854f-165cee581f0c" "answer-63c50681-0310-54e1-a7ce-97fde423a4b0" "answer-99607e2e-69b1-5c13-81d9-aae71cd65b14" "answer-00b575c8-36c5-5013-80f6-ee1498a6faf2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01915aac-1c2e-585b-999e-bd689a77b856" :answer/id #uuid "01915aac-1c2e-585b-999e-bd689a77b856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d11c7d00-ca24-5099-854f-165cee581f0c" :answer/id #uuid "d11c7d00-ca24-5099-854f-165cee581f0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63c50681-0310-54e1-a7ce-97fde423a4b0" :answer/id #uuid "63c50681-0310-54e1-a7ce-97fde423a4b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99607e2e-69b1-5c13-81d9-aae71cd65b14" :answer/id #uuid "99607e2e-69b1-5c13-81d9-aae71cd65b14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00b575c8-36c5-5013-80f6-ee1498a6faf2" :answer/id #uuid "00b575c8-36c5-5013-80f6-ee1498a6faf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172056 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7e0b385-be5e-5415-b9aa-b210f7036677"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c7e0b385-be5e-5415-b9aa-b210f7036677" :question/id #uuid "c7e0b385-be5e-5415-b9aa-b210f7036677" :question/math-academy-id "q-161046" :question/problem "$$\nr(z,\\theta )=⟨\\text{__________},\\,\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $r(z,\\theta )$ above parametrizes the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y=\\sqrt{z-1}$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $z$-axis for $z\\in [1,10].$ What is the first component of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/04/04de4ea7dc617be1429c596812ce4f450c2cdaafd8d94d86f75e68a6743acba9.png)\n\n \n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $y=f(z)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $z$-axis has the position vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨f(z)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,z\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $y=f(z)=\\sqrt{z-1}\\ge 0$ for all $z\\in [1,10].$ \n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(z,\\theta )=⟨\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,z\\in [1,10],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $r$ is $\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-741e1c0e-e03a-5747-adb3-6e19f296eab1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-741e1c0e-e03a-5747-adb3-6e19f296eab1" :answer-field/id #uuid "741e1c0e-e03a-5747-adb3-6e19f296eab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2477c6cb-c064-5421-afe0-a8e5def630d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b069f039-452f-5174-ba92-cb3de1a0b57b" "answer-e118469f-bcd0-5c50-aab2-4bee0d032ed1" "answer-39a9acae-d6a3-505a-9113-cf64e8d3f284" "answer-7a9ef23b-b0fd-5e83-9f3b-d5c76fdedc47" "answer-2477c6cb-c064-5421-afe0-a8e5def630d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b069f039-452f-5174-ba92-cb3de1a0b57b" :answer/id #uuid "b069f039-452f-5174-ba92-cb3de1a0b57b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\sqrt{z}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e118469f-bcd0-5c50-aab2-4bee0d032ed1" :answer/id #uuid "e118469f-bcd0-5c50-aab2-4bee0d032ed1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(z-1)^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39a9acae-d6a3-505a-9113-cf64e8d3f284" :answer/id #uuid "39a9acae-d6a3-505a-9113-cf64e8d3f284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(z-1){sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a9ef23b-b0fd-5e83-9f3b-d5c76fdedc47" :answer/id #uuid "7a9ef23b-b0fd-5e83-9f3b-d5c76fdedc47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2477c6cb-c064-5421-afe0-a8e5def630d0" :answer/id #uuid "2477c6cb-c064-5421-afe0-a8e5def630d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157598 :question/problem "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{50}$ is a sample of size $n=50$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =30$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=9,$ what is $\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu .$ Then, the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{X}$ is an unbiased estimator of $\\mu ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu .\n$$\n\nTherefore, since the population mean $\\mu =30,$ we have that $\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=30.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153832 :answer-field/correct 17592186153837 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-bf53dea8-f555-5d67-8b1f-60c3c23bf32f" :activity/id #uuid "bf53dea8-f555-5d67-8b1f-60c3c23bf32f" :activity/title "Quiz 1" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-1c778fa9-95bd-5205-85c3-55aecdf8bb5a" "step-cc7f63aa-08fc-552c-9ea6-c824a10e6a14" "step-a5c706c5-3ca3-5218-b66a-dfcd2740c675" "step-c3276151-f349-520e-b3ce-b128b261e8d4" "step-69dce80a-516d-5704-9e0c-f853f687f3c7" "step-26b7b285-8b87-524a-acc3-8f6ad9b2bc51" "step-5c8fa560-f511-5232-9190-5ad13dbecf87" "step-982b4c12-887f-5e66-8054-16e26a5f9fff"] :activity/first-step "step-1c778fa9-95bd-5205-85c3-55aecdf8bb5a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-1c778fa9-95bd-5205-85c3-55aecdf8bb5a" :step/id #uuid "1c778fa9-95bd-5205-85c3-55aecdf8bb5a" :step/content 17592186134551 :step/next "step-cc7f63aa-08fc-552c-9ea6-c824a10e6a14" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cc7f63aa-08fc-552c-9ea6-c824a10e6a14" :step/id #uuid "cc7f63aa-08fc-552c-9ea6-c824a10e6a14" :step/content "question-2dd7bee1-71b3-5685-9b9f-df2041d5d283" :step/next "step-a5c706c5-3ca3-5218-b66a-dfcd2740c675" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a5c706c5-3ca3-5218-b66a-dfcd2740c675" :step/id #uuid "a5c706c5-3ca3-5218-b66a-dfcd2740c675" :step/content 17592186415681 :step/next "step-c3276151-f349-520e-b3ce-b128b261e8d4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c3276151-f349-520e-b3ce-b128b261e8d4" :step/id #uuid "c3276151-f349-520e-b3ce-b128b261e8d4" :step/content 17592186241072 :step/next "step-69dce80a-516d-5704-9e0c-f853f687f3c7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-69dce80a-516d-5704-9e0c-f853f687f3c7" :step/id #uuid "69dce80a-516d-5704-9e0c-f853f687f3c7" :step/content "question-dfb0578c-1343-53e2-a376-085feaa6ce26" :step/next "step-26b7b285-8b87-524a-acc3-8f6ad9b2bc51" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-26b7b285-8b87-524a-acc3-8f6ad9b2bc51" :step/id #uuid "26b7b285-8b87-524a-acc3-8f6ad9b2bc51" :step/content "question-c7e0b385-be5e-5415-b9aa-b210f7036677" :step/next "step-5c8fa560-f511-5232-9190-5ad13dbecf87" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5c8fa560-f511-5232-9190-5ad13dbecf87" :step/id #uuid "5c8fa560-f511-5232-9190-5ad13dbecf87" :step/content 17592186389442 :step/next "step-982b4c12-887f-5e66-8054-16e26a5f9fff" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-982b4c12-887f-5e66-8054-16e26a5f9fff" :step/id #uuid "982b4c12-887f-5e66-8054-16e26a5f9fff" :step/content 17592186157598 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110659 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-194005bc-f62b-59e9-a404-19d959ce797e" "question-0ada8c79-b2a0-5a2c-836a-ac533831ba5c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110297 :question/problem "Calculate $\\left(\\dfrac{2x}{3}\\right)^4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2x}{3})}^{4}=\\frac{(2x)^{4}}{{3}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2x)^{4}}{{3}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{4}{x}^{4}}{{3}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{16{x}^{4}}{81} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110660 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3cbc76cf-73cd-53cf-89d7-15a5f1f46f2b" "question-12eb7643-9611-58a5-926c-4abbb115bd9f" "question-2b75a1b6-f44a-5a5a-8342-d11fe3f5f88d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110298 :question/problem "Simplify $\\left(\\dfrac{y}{2}\\right)^3 \\left(\\dfrac{2y}{3}\\right)^2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{2})}^{3}{(\\frac{2y}{3})}^{2}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{(2y)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{(2y)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{2}{y}^{2}}{9} & = \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\cdot \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & = \\\\ \\frac{4{y}^{(3+2)}}{72} & = \\\\ \\frac{4{y}^{5}}{72} & = \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{5}}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-194005bc-f62b-59e9-a404-19d959ce797e" :question/id #uuid "194005bc-f62b-59e9-a404-19d959ce797e" :question/math-academy-id "q-51811" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${(\\frac{wt}{2})}^{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{wt}{2})}^{4}=\\frac{(wt)^{4}}{{2}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(wt)^{4}}{{2}^{4}}=\\frac{{w}^{4}{t}^{4}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6f50fe2-5ffa-5708-971c-1bb1bfe98ebd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6f50fe2-5ffa-5708-971c-1bb1bfe98ebd" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6f50fe2-5ffa-5708-971c-1bb1bfe98ebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e4f48316-1ccd-51df-9650-8fc2b23a63cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc8f9b65-2c81-5b98-b118-1c5ba0a1575c" "answer-ed43c60b-0204-50f4-9b2a-36acab6d2adc" "answer-e4f48316-1ccd-51df-9650-8fc2b23a63cc" "answer-f73f0d60-406c-5725-9667-6ef7590867ff" "answer-da04446e-ee47-5f61-b14d-4d21c44d682c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc8f9b65-2c81-5b98-b118-1c5ba0a1575c" :answer/i